# cdc_snapshot.sby — the starvation crossing's replacement, proved as a protocol.
#
# WHY THIS PROOF EXISTS
#
# The shell sampled a 64-bit vid_clk counter directly into gpu_clk and checked
# AFTERWARDS whether it had moved. Measured across four composed fits that
# touched nothing in that path, its hold slack read -0.952 FAIL, +0.254 pass,
# +0.259 pass, -0.728 FAIL: 1.2 ns of swing on placement alone, which made the
# whole shell timing verdict nondeterministic.
#
# The replacement is a toggle-handshake mailbox. What has to be true of it is a
# PROTOCOL claim, not a value claim, so it is proved rather than watched.
#
# WHAT IS PROVED (properties live in the DUT under `ifdef FORMAL):
#   the source cannot touch the held value while a snapshot is uncollected;
#   a publish while busy raises a STICKY overflow and never silently drops;
#   the destination never fabricates a snapshot;
#   the acknowledgement names the request actually consumed;
#   the valid latch never retracts.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVED, stated so nobody reads more into a green than is there:
#   METASTABILITY. No formal tool establishes it; that is the three-flop
#   synchronizer's job and a settling-time argument.
#   DIFFERING CLOCK RATES. This harness drives both domains from one clock, so
#   the synchronizers degrade to plain delays. The rate case -- a destination
#   slower than the publish rate, which is exactly what ovf_o is for -- needs a
#   simulation test at randomised relative phase. It is a REAL GAP and is
#   recorded as one in design/formal_runs.yml rather than implied away.
#
# TWO TASKS, both required (ledger rule V16):
#   bmc   — the assertions hold to the depth below.
#   cover — the antecedents are REACHABLE. Every assertion here is an
#           implication, and a machine that never publishes satisfies all of
#           them while proving nothing. The covers demand a publish, a
#           collection, a busy window, an overflow, and TWO snapshots in
#           sequence.
#
# DEPTH. The longest causal chain is publish -> req toggle -> three destination
# flops -> capture+ack -> three source flops -> busy clears -> second publish,
# which is 2 + 3 + 1 + 3 + 1 = 10 steps; c_two_snaps needs a second pass through
# it. 32 gives that with room and keeps the run trivial.

# SCOPE-TOTAL: every assertion here is STEP-LOCAL -- each relates the current
# state to $past(state) one clock earlier, with no horizon assumption and no
# quantity that accumulates toward a bound. Raising the depth cannot reach a
# state the proof did not already cover at every step, so there is nothing
# for an a_scope_* guard to fire on.
#
# The depth exists for the COVERS, not the asserts: c_two_snaps-style
# reachability needs the full publish -> 3 sync flops -> capture+ack -> 3
# sync flops -> busy clear -> publish loop, about 10 steps, and 32 gives that
# twice over. A cover that becomes reachable at a greater depth would be a
# missing cover, not a broken bound.
#
# Contrast field_seq_bound, where the depth IS the claim: a_progress bounds
# busy_cnt, so raising the depth past its derivation would silently re-scope
# what PASS means and its a_scope_short_program_window exists to refuse that.
#
[tasks]
bmc
cover

[options]
bmc:   mode bmc
bmc:   depth 32
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 32
expect pass

[engines]
btor btormc

[script]
read_slang --top zhao_cdc_snapshot -DFORMAL zhao_cdc_snapshot.sv
prep -top zhao_cdc_snapshot

[files]
../../fpga/rtl/common/zhao_cdc_snapshot.sv
